      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Poach chicken thighs in 600ml water with a pinch of salt for 20 minutes. Remove and shred. Keep the stock."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend cashews with soaked bread, milk, and 100ml stock until completely smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in a large frying pan over medium heat. Fry onion for 8 minutes until soft. Add garlic and turmeric, fry for 2 more minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add chilli powder if using. Pour in the cashew-bread paste and stir well. The mixture will be very thick."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add remaining stock gradually, stirring until the sauce is smooth and pourable. Simmer for 8 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir in the shredded chicken. Taste for salt. Simmer for 5 more minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Serve over white rice. Garnish with a black olive or sliced boiled egg if you like."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Sauce is too thick and stiff",
              "cause": "Too much bread or not enough liquid added.",
              "fix": "Add warm stock a ladleful at a time, stirring after each addition, until the sauce flows freely."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Sauce has a grainy texture",
              "cause": "Cashews were not blended long enough.",
              "fix": "Return the sauce base to the blender with a splash of warm milk and blend for a full 2 minutes."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Colour is dull",
              "cause": "Not enough turmeric for the golden hue.",
              "fix": "Stir in a pinch more turmeric at the end. The sauce should be a warm, deep yellow."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Aji de gallina is one of Peru's great national dishes. Its origins lie in the colonial period when Spanish nuns adapted European bread-thickened sauces using Andean yellow chillies. The dish evolved over centuries into something distinctly Peruvian. Today it is eaten in every class and region of the country. Lima's restaurants serve elaborate versions, but the home cooking version, made with whatever chillies and nuts are available, is the one most Peruvians grew up eating."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
